* Absence proofs\non Cardano
** The problem
*** A validator sees one transaction\nand nothing else
*** No lookup, no chain access
*** Citation is the only channel\nfor on-chain state
** The structure
*** Sorted linked list of UTxOs
*** Key minted into the asset name,\nimmutable
*** Link in the inline datum,\nmutable
*** Root is -inf, a None link is +inf
** The proof
*** One covering node,\nsupplied as a reference input
*** key < target < link,\nboth bounds strict
*** O(1), whatever the list length
*** Sanctioned party: no gap exists,\nso the proof cannot be built
** Why user input is safe
*** The builder supplies an index
*** The ledger supplies the contents
*** Sufficiency, not correctness
*** Forgery fails on the NFT,\nthe datum or the address pin
** Where trust sits
*** insert_ascending keeps\nthe chain exact
*** Links can never skip a member
*** Paid once per sanction,\nnot once per transfer
** Building it
*** Parties are stake credentials
*** Actions matched positionally
*** Ledger sorts inputs before\nscripts run
*** Adjacent parties sharing a node\nauthenticate once
@endmindmap
